# ── Derived data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything under data/ is reproducible: calibrated/ (uncal/rate pools) re-downloads from
# MAST, stage1/ stage2/ mosaics/ regenerate from scripts/reduce_nircam.py. Provenance lives
# in info/*.json. B1938+666 alone is ~80 GB of uncal, so none of it enters git history.
#
# data/cutouts is the deliberate exception (as in the HST repo): the final science stamps
# are small and carry the hand-drawn, non-regenerable masks and positions.
data/*
!data/cutouts/
!data/qc/
# QC renders, as in the HST repo (2026-10-04): cutout_positions.png is a view OF the tracked
# positions JSON (rebuilt by make_positions.py --overlays-only), and cutout.png a plain render
# of the tracked sci stamp (rebuilt by make_cutouts.py). Neither is a product, and every
# re-cut adds a ~0.5-1.2 MB version to history. Variant renders (cutout_<variant>.png) are not
# covered: there are none yet, and a cutout_*.png rule would also catch future _dataset.png
# and _mask_arcs.png, which the HST repo keeps tracked.
data/cutouts/**/*_positions.png
data/cutouts/**/cutout.png

# ── Generated / local ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
output/
diagnostics/
/local/
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
.venv/
# CRDS cache and STPSF data live under data/ (ignored above) -- see AGENTS.md, Environment.

# personal venv + SSH/rsync aliases, as colibre_VDisp/activate.sh
activate_local.sh
